          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Under cabinet lighting is one of the cheapest upgrades that changes how a kitchen works every day, but only if you choose in the right order. Settle the power source first, then pick bars for counters, pucks for display and COB tape for glossy stone, and insist on a listed CRI of 90 with a color temperature that matches your ceiling lights.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
